In short (not legally binding: only the sections below are)

  ARCHIMED is free and its source code is available to read. You may use,
  copy and modify it for your own use, personal or professional. You may not
  redistribute it, sell it, or build it into another piece of software. What
  you create with ARCHIMED is yours.


Section 1 — Definitions

  "Licensor": SearaDesign, holder of the copyright in the Software.

  "Software": the ARCHIMED program in all its forms (source code, object
  code, executables, installers), together with its documentation, modules,
  file templates, images and texts, as published by the Licensor under this
  license, including later versions.

  "You": the natural or legal person exercising the rights granted by this
  license.

  "Modified Version": any work that reproduces all or part of the Software,
  whether modified or not (adaptation, translation, correction, adding or
  removing a module, extracting a part).

  "Distribute": to make the Software or a Modified Version, in whole or in
  part, available to any person other than You, in any form and by any means
  (download, public code repository, physical media, app store, package
  registry, direct sending, remote access), free of charge or for a fee.

  "Your Creations": the content You produce by using the Software (projects,
  the code of your own programs, mods, images, texts, documents), together
  with the files the Software generates in those projects.

  "Own Use": use by You, for Your own needs, personal or professional. For a
  legal person, internal use by its employees and agents on its behalf is
  part of its Own Use and is not Distribution.


Section 2 — Rights granted

  2.1 The Licensor grants You, free of charge, on a non-exclusive basis,
  worldwide and for the full term of copyright protection in the Software,
  and for Your Own Use only:

    a) the right to reproduce the Software: install, load, display, run and
       copy it, in as many copies as Your Own Use requires, backups included;

    b) the right to adapt the Software: modify, correct, translate and
       arrange it and create Modified Versions, including compiling Your own
       version of the application;

    c) the right to reproduce and use the Modified Versions You create,
       within the same limits.

  2.2 Contributions. You may submit modifications of the Software
  ("Contributions") to the Licensor through its official repository,
  https://github.com/Kaylloggs/SDAI-ARCHIMED, for example as a pull request.
  Sending a Contribution to the Licensor is not Distribution. By submitting a
  Contribution, You declare that You are its author or hold the necessary
  rights, and You grant the Licensor, free of charge, on a non-exclusive
  basis, worldwide and for the full term of copyright protection, in order
  to include it in the Software and exploit the Software under this license
  or any other license of its choice:

    a) the right to reproduce the Contribution;
    b) the right to perform it and communicate it to the public;
    c) the right to adapt, modify, correct and translate it;
    d) the right to distribute it, free of charge or for a fee;
    e) the right to grant third parties all or part of these rights.

  2.3 Hosting platform. Where the Software is published on a platform whose
  terms of use allow its users to view it and to make a copy of it on that
  same platform (for example a "fork" on GitHub), these actions are allowed
  within the limits of those terms. Such a copy remains subject to this
  license and may only serve Your Own Use or the preparation of a
  Contribution.


Section 3 — Prohibitions

  Unless the Licensor gives prior written consent, You may not:

    a) Distribute the Software or a Modified Version, in whole or in part, in
       any form (source code, executable, installer), free of charge or for a
       fee;

    b) sell, rent or lend the Software or a Modified Version, sublicense it,
       or earn revenue by making it available, including by offering it as a
       remotely accessible service;

    c) build all or part of the Software into another piece of software,
       product or service made available to third parties, whether its code
       is closed or open;

    d) remove or alter the copyright, license or author notices contained in
       the Software;

    e) use the names "ARCHIMED", "SDAI ARCHIMED", "SearaDesign" or the
       Software's logo to name or promote a Modified Version or another
       product.


Section 4 — Your Creations

  4.1 The Licensor claims no rights in Your Creations. This license places
  no restriction on them: You may use, publish, distribute and sell them
  freely.

  4.2 The files the Software creates in Your projects (for example the files
  of a Minecraft mod project created by Mod Studio, generated code, textures,
  exported images), including when they reuse templates shipped with the
  Software, are part of Your Creations. The Licensor allows You to
  reproduce, modify and distribute them with Your Creations, without
  restriction.

  4.3 Content produced by third-party services (AI providers, websites)
  remains subject to those services' terms. Third-party files placed in Your
  projects (for example the Gradle Wrapper) remain subject to their own
  license.


Section 5 — Third-party components

  The Software contains third-party components under their own licenses,
  whose notices are kept with them (for example
  src/core/engine/prompts/caveman.LICENSE and
  src-tauri/src/modules/jobagent/engine/LICENSE.jobspy). This license only
  covers the parts in which the Licensor holds the rights; it does not
  restrict the rights that those components' licenses grant You in them.


Section 6 — Rights granted to You by law

  Nothing in this license limits the rights that the law grants the user of
  a software program without the rightsholder's permission, in particular
  those provided by Article L122-6-1 of the French Intellectual Property Code
  (backup copy, observing and studying how the program works, decompilation
  for interoperability, under the conditions set by that article).


Section 7 — Earlier versions

  Copies of the Software that the Licensor published under the MIT License,
  namely the versions released up to and including 0.6.0 and the states of
  the source code published before this license was added to the official
  repository on 26 September 2026, remain under the MIT License. This license
  applies to everything the Licensor publishes after that addition, starting
  with version 0.7.0.


Section 8 — Termination

  8.1 Any breach of this license automatically terminates, without further
  formality, the rights it grants You.

  8.2 If it is Your first breach and You cure it within thirty (30) days of
  the Licensor notifying You of it, Your rights are reinstated.

  8.3 Upon termination, You must stop using the Software and Modified
  Versions and destroy all copies. Sections 4, 5, 6, 9 and 11 survive.


Section 9 — No warranty and liability

  9.1 The Software is provided free of charge, "as is", without warranty of
  any kind, express or implied, including of proper operation, fitness for a
  particular purpose or absence of errors, to the fullest extent permitted by
  applicable law.

  9.2 To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the Licensor is not
  liable for any damage arising from the use of, or inability to use, the
  Software, including loss of data, nor for actions carried out by the AI
  assistants or third-party services You connect to the Software.

  9.3 This section does not limit the Licensor's liability where the law
  forbids limiting it, in particular in case of gross negligence or wilful
  misconduct, and does not deprive consumers of rights granted to them by
  mandatory provisions.


Section 10 — Other permissions

  Any use not allowed by this license, in particular Distribution, sale or
  inclusion in another product, requires the Licensor's prior written
  consent. Requests are made to the Licensor through the Software's official
  repository.


Section 11 — Governing law, language and severability

  11.1 This license is governed by French law.

  11.2 It is written in French and in English. If the two versions differ,
  the French version prevails.

  11.3 If any provision of this license is held void or unenforceable, the
  other provisions remain in force.
